														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1392123">
									

<p>There's a lot I like about this concept, but the article has a fair ammount of fat to trim, and something is bothering me about that end note. With as much information as there is to cover, the length will be understandably hard to control; however, if you can pare it down and do something for the pacing / flow, I can easily see myself upvoting.</p>
<p>Aside: I'm somewhat reminded of the Kandra from the Mistborn trilogy. Based on the wetsuits it seems that an exoskeleton helps the -1 instances out quite a bit; it wouldn't be as secure, but could the same effect be achieved by providing them an endoskeleton to wrap around?</p>
<p>Likewise, given that there are no longer distinctions between types of tissue, is there anything to prevent -1 instances from eatting to excess in order to increase their usable mass? Or do they even eat?</p>

