			<div class="content" id="post-content-1392137">
									

<blockquote>
<p>There's a lot I like about this concept, but the article has a fair ammount of fat to trim, and something is bothering me about that end note. With as much information as &gt; there is to cover, the length will be understandably hard to control; however, if you can pare it down and do something for the pacing / flow, I can easily see myself<br />
upvoting.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I agree with you that I had to include a lot of information and it felt a bit clunky to me when it was all down. (As an aside: If someone reading this likes the concept and feels like they can tighten this up, PM me please.) I added the end note to elaborate on the idea that this was developed as a joint project involving the Foundation, and others may be more enthusiastic about it than the Foundation researchers who have seen it close-up. Maybe there is a better way to do that?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Aside: I'm somewhat reminded of the Kandra from the Mistborn trilogy. Based on the wetsuits it seems that an exoskeleton helps the -1 instances out quite a bit; it<br />
wouldn't be as secure, but could the same effect be achieved by providing them an endoskeleton to wrap around?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I didn't have anything in mind from another canon when writing this, but am not surprised that something like it would be out there. An endoskeleton would work&#8230;I chose the containment suits over an endoskeleton for the (unstated) reason that it hides the form of the -1s that can't transform. It also keeps them from merging into -2s when the researchers don't want them doing that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Likewise, given that there are no longer distinctions between types of tissue, is there anything to prevent -1 instances from eatting to excess in order to increase<br />
their usable mass? Or do they even eat?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I thought about adding something on this point, but didn't want to make the SCP even longer. I was thinking of saying that -1s eat enough to maintain their mass, but have a high enough metabolism to not increase it. -2s, on the other hand, can grow through excessive food. I'd like to keep the -1s human-sized, while the -2s can grow indefinitely large.</p>

							</div>

