														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1392329">
									

<p>Why exactly did the Foundation collaborate with ANYONE in assisting to create a potential SCP from products/parts of any other held SCP? When and why was a &quot;general&quot; involved? It completely breaks what little of a collective canon we have, how essentially the Foundation is secret to any other organizations to the greatest extent possible, let alone any militaries (implied by the last note). Why would <em>any</em> object with an SCP designation be &quot;in dispute&quot; for whether or not it should be handed to other organizations? Also, why should the human byproducts of the SCP be allowed to participate in official Foundation activities? Why are they being let to live beyond specific study purposes, rather than being destroyed as per normal Foundation procedure? I really don't like any of the article past the description's explanation of the relationship between -1s and -2s.</p>
<p>Until these are answered or resolved to my liking, I'm keeping this at a downvote.</p>
<p>This article isn't without merit, I like the core element of it. However, something about the last part feels OOC and the aliens seem a little bit corny (thinking of the Darloks from MoO) and frankly unrealistic to the canon as it stands.</p>

