<blockquote>
<p>When and why was a &quot;general&quot; involved? It completely breaks what little of a collective canon we have, how essentially the Foundation is secret to any other organizations to the greatest extent possible, let alone any militaries (implied by the last note).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>First off, as oft-stated, there is no canon per se. That said, most articles/tales that address the Foundation's dealings with external forces and organizations have it acknowledged, however quietly, by a variety of world governments and militaries. The US, Soviet, Nazi, Chinese, British, Iranian, and Canadian governments come to mind off the top of my head. No formal and definitive origin story has ever been definitively established for the Foundation, though several possible and mutually contradictory stories do exist. In at least some of them, the Foundation was originally created as a partially military organization. Similarly, the GOC is often shown as being in league with governments. So, I think it probably safe to assume (at least major) governments are aware of the Foundation, though the general population most certainly would not be.</p>
<p>Second of all, it's been established that some parts of the Foundation itself are structured militarily. At least one General (Bowe) has been established as being part of the Foundation. I don't think this is what the author was meaning to imply here, but it's worth noting.</p>

