			<div class="content" id="post-content-1392362">
									

<p>Here's how it goes in my version of the (non) canon:</p>
<p>The Foundation is not quite as secret as it would like to be. It's known at high levels of the military and some other government organizations.</p>
<p>It doesn't normally cooperate in this way with other organizations, but the O5's can pretty much do what they want, and are not always exempt from politics. One way to think of this SCP is as a rogue project sponsored by one or two O5's, that the rest choose to ignore. This is not a good thing; it's asking for trouble; in fact, I'm presenting this SCP as an example of why it might not be good for the Foundation to act as R &amp; D for other organizations. The Foundation wants to contain the stuff; the other organizations want to use it.</p>
<p>The Foundation is keeping a population of -1's and -2's around for experiments&#8230;to figure out their capabilities and how to defend against them&#8230;and they're pack rats in general. It's the same reason they keep all sorts of other dangerous living SCPs around. Most of them are former D-class, and as such are not involved in operations. The Foundation is very suspicious of the couple of non-D-class converted (a hint that there is something not quite right about this SCP's effects).</p>

