			<div class="content" id="post-content-1392386">
									

<p>I love the <em>spirit</em> of this article, but the execution could use some work. Some phrases that especially bother me:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(one D-Class previously assigned to SCP-███ clean-up duty unsuccessfully attempted to escape by simulating SCP-███ and attacking his guards)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is this really necessary? Removing this sentence from its paragraph does not impede the understanding of the skip's effect, but improves the overall tone of the article.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and maintain the change voluntarily for an indefinite period.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Form conversion is physically tiring, and SCP-1961-1 subjects have not been able to retain human form for a period longer than four hours</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Inconsistency, should be fixed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They are a new, alien, life-form that considers itself superior to us.<br />
They will be our masters, not our servants.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I <em>like</em> the O5 note, and think that it's a good final touch for an already good idea, but those two particular sentences strike me as cheesy.</p>
<p>Once again, I don't think that the <em>concept</em> needs any changes at all. This could well be the best thing that can be done to the transformation mirror idea. But the execution just not as good as the concept. No vote for now.</p>

