														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1392734">
									

<p>This is a good SCP. Some minor points, though, mostly to do with this paragraph:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is designed to emit a mixture of ████████ and ██████ radiation and concentrate the rays on a human subject, previously injected with [DATA EXPUNGED], [DATA EXPUNGED], and SCP-███ blood. The intent of the procedure is to give the treated subject the power to modify his/her physical form at will, and maintain the change voluntarily for an indefinite period.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>- &quot;Data&quot; is plural; you only need to write &quot;Data Expunged&quot; once.<br />
- The idea of a purposefully-designed SCP sits badly with me, although I realise this opinion is not universal.<br />
- Simply injecting the subject with the blood of another SCP seems overly simplistic. Unless SCP-███ is an existing SCP specifically characterised by having blood that can somehow transform its subject, or at the very least not cause some kind of horrible reaction (as happens when you give someone the wrong blood type, for example) I'd make it so that the blood needed to undergo some kind of processing first. Otherwise it just starts sounding like alchemy.</p>

							</div>

								
					
